#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps.md:8
msgid ""
"Here is how the standard dependency tree of a modern procedural macro crate "
"is structured:"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps.md:27
msgid "Each library builds on top of the layer below."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps.md:28
msgid ""
"Using `syn` and `quote` increases macro build times slightly, but greatly "
"simplifies implementation, making macro code safer and much easier to "
"maintain."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps.md:34
msgid ""
"Explain that `proc_macro` is provided by the standard distribution, but is "
"restricted to compiler execution."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps.md:36
msgid ""
"`proc_macro2` is a standard third-party crate that replicates all "
"`proc_macro` types, but does not depend on the compiler's private internals. "
"This is why testing libraries or other tools can work with token streams."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps.md:39
msgid ""
"`syn` and `quote` operate fully on `proc_macro2` types, allowing seamless "
"integration."
msgstr ""
